sections.content:
Morning on awakening. From any motion. Lying;
  stooping; after stools; urinating. Cold air, and after
  washing in water. Winter. Standing.

Fear; he will never get well, nor bear any medicine;
  of being poisoned. Wants many things, pleased with
  nothing.

Copious, ropy expectoration, in a.m. in
   aged persons. Catarrh of chest; chest weak, hemoptysis;
   mucus expelled with difficulty.

Twitching of the facial muscles. Cramps in lips;
   lips hot. Left cheek red. Flushes of the face, jaundiced
   color. Embarrassed look. Lock-jaw in newborn.

Frequent emission of clear watery urine;
   deposit turbid, clay-coloured sediment. Sensation of
   burning in the glans during and after urination.

Dull pressure or feeling of a heavy load
   on shoulders. Stiffness of nape and neck down back;
   pain, < motion.

