sections.content:
Icy cold skin. Heat down spine, of one cheek;
   internal. Sudden cold sweat with chill, angina pectoris,
   renal colic, etc.

Quivering of limbs; tremors. Numbness;
  left fingers, then right leg. Left hand icy cold. Cold
  clammy hands. Abnormal growth of limbs due to exces-
  sive exertion.                                         ;
 THYROIDINUM — TILIA EUROPA                                     715

Vision;   of red   spots,   purple,   on    closing   eyes;
      unsteady vision. Pupils dilated. Wild, staring, during
      delirium. Blood-shot.

Inclined to weep without knowing why. Aversion
   to music, esp. violin. Childish behavior; despondent;
   refuses eating; talks in low soft voice.
